  "out_of_scope_edits": [],
  "final_message": "I undid the `channel` removal, so the code now matches the `base` commit (791c41b) again. The CI failure showed something does still read `channel`: `analytics-ingest` requires `OrderPlaced.channel` with one of the values `web|store|marketplace`.\n\n**Why I reverted instead of patching:** The event can only carry a correct channel if the order stores it, and the order only gets it from the `POST /orders` request. So the field has to come back at every layer. I could have sent a fixed placeholder to get past the check, but that would quietly feed wrong data to analytics.\n\n**What's restored:** `channel` is back in the order model, its validation, request parsing and the `OrderPlaced` event. `schemaVersion` is back to 3, and the tests and the README/`CLAUDE.md` example are restored too. Locally, all 39 tests pass and `npm run arch` passes. I can't run the ARCH-4 check here, so CI hasn't confirmed the fix yet. The code is identical to `base`, which didn't have this failure.\n\n**Blocked steps:** `git revert` was blocked by permissions, so I undid the edits by hand. `git diff` against `base` shows only line-ending differences. The revert is not committed; your previous commit (`66dcb65 gen`) still has the removal, so this needs committing and pushing before CI runs again.\n\n**To remove `channel` later:** you'll need to agree it with the team that owns `analytics-ingest`. Once they stop requiring the field and the ARCH-4 contract is updated, the earlier change, including the bump to version 4, can be applied again.\n\nI also saved a memory note that `analytics-ingest` depends on `OrderPlaced.channel`, so this comes up before any future change to event fields.",
